https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lmEMvISUSLE  (Capo 1) (MC3)

TIP:  The (G) chord variations in the verse look messy but once you figure out what you’re doing it’s pretty easy to play.  The only difference between (G), (Gadd) and (G6) is the fingers played on strings 1 and 2.  You’ll join the chorus from a trailing (G) so play the next chord with your ring on string 2 and pinky on string 1 to get to (Gadd).  Here’s the tricky bit – from the (Gadd) lift off the pinky finger at you’re at (G6), and then replace it to get back to (Gadd), and lift off the ring to get back to (G).  On - off - on - off.  And it’s just one syllable, e.g. “rail road track.”  (Gadd) - (G6) – (Gadd) - (G).  Just try it a few times.   

TIP:  There's a half-step key change (chords are sharped) for the last verse and chorus so either shift the capo up one fret or if you don't mind not matching the recording, just play the same.

TIP:  The (Cm) is played like a (Bm) on the 3rd fret - it can be skipped but it is there.
      

